package li.velvetchat.app.ui

/**
 * the icon paths, as code rather than resources
 *
 * generated by `tools/icones-vers-kotlin.py` from the vector drawables that lived in
 * `res/drawable/`. do not edit by hand: the source is still the phosphor svgs, and the chain is
 * svg, vector drawable, this file
 *
 * why it is no longer a resource
 *
 * the 65 icons are one path each, in a 256 by 256 viewport, with no `fillType` and no gradient,
 * checked across all 65 before converting. compose can build an `ImageVector` from such a string in
 * common code (`addPathNodes`), so nothing forced us through `R.drawable` and `painterResource`
 *
 * what that unblocks: `Icone()` is called by nearly every screen in the app, and while it depended
 * on `R` none of them could leave `app-android`
 *
 * phosphor icons, mit licence. the attribution lives in the about screen, as the licence requires
 */
